> A hand-checkable likelihood reference

A uniform categorical distribution over65 classes gives negative log-likelihood log(65). For language/image models this is nats per predicted token; for a sequence tagger it is a single independent-token reference, not its CRF sequence likelihood.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/token_sampling_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto logp=dm::nn::log_softmax(dm::nn::zeros({1,65}),1);double computed=-logp.to_vector<double>()[0];std::print("| classes | native uniform NLL | analytic NLL |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n| 65 | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",computed,std::log(65.));dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(std::vector<double>{0,1},std::vector<double>{computed,std::log(65.)},"uniform NLL",{37,99,235}).ylim(0,std::log(65.)*1.2).title("token sampling uniform reference").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/token_sampling_worked.svg");}
```
