> Scope and provenance

Source partitions, fitting-only transformations, explicit update/generation loops and independent deployment guards are retained. Native preparation manifests record the recovered source hashes and protocol. The small models and samples are teaching experiments; no full-paper reproduction, benchmark ranking or unrecorded external parity is claimed.

> Compare how aggressively the samplers filter

The effective vocabulary is the inverse sum of squared token
probabilities at each generated step. A value of one denotes a
deterministic choice. Larger values indicate less concentrated
sampling distributions along that method’s own generated sequence.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/token_sampling_effective_vocabulary.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <array>
#include <filesystem>

int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  using dm::graphics::RGB;
  const std::string base = "build/recovered-language/models/token_sampling/source-protocol/";
  const auto steps = n::arange(1, 33).to_vector<double>();
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  for (const auto& [name, color] : std::array{
           std::pair{"greedy", RGB{51, 65, 85}}, std::pair{"temperature", RGB{37, 99, 235}},
           std::pair{"top_k", RGB{234, 88, 12}}, std::pair{"nucleus", RGB{22, 120, 68}}}) {
    for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz(base + name + ".npz")) {
      if (key == "probability") {
        const auto count = (1.0 / n::sum(n::square(value), {1})).to_vector<double>();
        plot.lines(steps, count, name, color);
      }
    }
  }
  const auto output = base + "effective_vocabulary.svg";
  plot.title("Effective vocabulary along each generated sequence")
      .x_label("Generated token").y_label("Inverse probability concentration").save_svg(output);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  std::filesystem::copy_file(output, "figures/token_sampling_effective_vocabulary.svg",
                             std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
}
